<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/18th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt</p><h1 class="enc-title">Moamoria rebellion</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1769–1805</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Moamoria rebellion was a series of uprisings against the Ahom kings of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assam">Assam</a> from 1769 to about 1805. It was led by disciples of the Moamara satra, a Vaishnavite monastery whose followers, many of them of low <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caste">caste</a> or tribal origin, had been persecuted by the court. The rebels twice seized the capital, Rangpur, and the conflict devastated the population and fatally weakened the kingdom.</p></div>
